From ada29e3e848f8b111ac75f3fa70f06f3e2549108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:08:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MP3PLAY: FILELEN reads the header before it scans

mpg123_scan() on every file was the pointer stutter in MP3GEM: sub-op 11
runs inside the guest's event loop, one file per tick, and a full scan of
a 5-minute MP3 is not a 250 ms job. A Xing/Info header or a CBR file gives
mpg123_length() an answer from the first frame, so ask for that first and
only scan when it comes back empty.

Applies on top of "MP3PLAY: sub-op 11".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MGcLwq6U6E1QhD3W3PzuF7
---
 platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c b/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c
index dd3d560..ee5846e 100755
--- a/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c
+++ b/platforms/atari/audio/dmasnd_hdmi.c
@@ -575,12 +575,16 @@ long dmasnd_mp3_filelen(const char *host_path)
         mpg123_getformat(mh, &rate, &channels, &enc) == MPG123_OK && rate > 0) {
         off_t frames;
 
-        mpg123_scan(mh);
+        /* A Xing/Info header or a CBR file answers from the first frame;
+         * only a VBR file with no header needs the whole thing read. This
+         * runs inside the guest's event loop, one file per tick, so the
+         * cheap path matters. */
         frames = mpg123_length(mh);
-        if (frames > 0)
-            secs = (long)(frames / rate);
-        else
-            secs = 0;
+        if (frames <= 0) {
+            mpg123_scan(mh);
+            frames = mpg123_length(mh);
+        }
+        secs = (frames > 0) ? (long)(frames / rate) : 0;
         mpg123_close(mh);
     }
     mpg123_delete(mh);
